The `Init()` method is responsible for setting up the screen and initializing the necessary components and data structures. It is called from the `Start()` method, which is a Unity method that is automatically called when the script instance is being loaded.

The reason why the lists (`inputFields` and `correctChars`) are filled only during the `Init()` method is that this method is responsible for instantiating the input fields and text objects based on the provided `wordsWithMissingChars` list. It iterates through each `WordWithMissingChars` object, creates the necessary input fields and text objects, and populates the `inputFields` and `correctChars` lists accordingly.

