This script is responsible for creating a screen where the user has to fill in missing characters in a set of words. It uses prefabs for input fields, text elements, and word parent GameObjects. The spacing between characters is controlled by the `elementSpacing` field, which is assigned to the `spacing` property of the `HorizontalLayoutGroup` component added to each word parent GameObject.

The script also handles checking the user's input, displaying a failed message if any input is incorrect, and invoking an event when the entire sentence is correct.

Sure, we can modify the script to create the words without using a `HorizontalLayoutGroup`. Instead, we'll position the input fields and text elements manually using their `RectTransform` positions. Here's the modified version of the script:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;
using Screens.Bases;
using TMPro;
using UnityEngine;
using UnityEngine.Serialization;
using UnityEngine.UI;

namespace Screens
{
    [Serializable]
    public class WordWithMissingChars
    {
        public string word;
