To ensure that the keyboard remains active when moving to the next input field on mobile, you can explicitly activate the next input field after setting its value. This can be done by calling `ActivateInputField` on the next input field.

Here's how you can modify the `OnFieldValueChanged` method to ensure the keyboard stays active:

```csharp
private void OnFieldValueChanged(InputField inputField)
{
    int currentFieldIndex = inputFields.IndexOf(inputField);
    if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(inputField.text) && currentFieldIndex < inputFields.Count - 1)
    {
        // Activate the next input field
        StartCoroutine(ActivateNextInputField(inputFields[currentFieldIndex + 1]));
    }

    if (inputFields.All(field => !string.IsNullOrEmpty(field.text)))
    {
        NextButton.interactable = true; // Enable the next button when all fields are filled
        fakeNextButton.interactable = true; // Enable the fake next button when all fields are filled
    }
